192 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Warm up \0502\0553 min\051\n\nTell me about yourself\nTell me a bit about your daily routine \024 do you cook yourself or do you have help at home\077\nWho mostly handles the kitchen \024 you\054 your partner\054 or the cook\057helper\077\n\nCore \05015\05520 min\051\n\n3\056 Walk me through the last time you ran out of something at home \024 what happened\054 how did you find out\077\n\n4\056 Who told you \024 and when exactly did they tell you\077 Like\054 same day you needed it\054 or before\077\n\n5\056 What did you do immediately after finding out\077\n\n6\056 How did that make you feel in that moment \024 was it a big deal or just a minor inconvenience\077\n\n7\056 How often does this happen in a month\054 roughly\077\n\n8\056 Have you ever tried any system to track what\047s running low at home \024 a list\054 an app\054 anything\077 How did that go\077\nLead time specific \0505\0557 min\051\n\n9\056 If an app had warned you 3 days before that item was going to run out \024 would you have acted on it\054 or ignored it\077\n\n10\056 How early would that warning need to come for you to actually do something about it \024 not too early\054 not too late\077\n\n11\056 What would make you trust that warning enough to reorder before your cook even mentions it\077\nWrap up\n\n12\056 Is there anything about how you manage groceries at home that you think I\047d be surprised to hear\077)
     /K [ 1 ]
     /P 193 0 R
     /Pg 190 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
